## How this stage runs (orchestrator-owned — see `shared/GOVERNANCE-CORE.md` §6)
1. `gov.py state` refreshes `{{ factory.paths.module.state_dir }}/`; the brief = `references/ENGINE.md` rendered with `profile` + `factory` + `stage` + the state files.
2. The lane dispatches the brief{% if stage.dialogue %} as a converging dialogue ({{ factory.lanes[stage.lane].dialogue.max_rounds }} rounds max, converge on *{{ factory.lanes[stage.lane].dialogue.converge_on }}*){% endif %}.
3. Artifacts are written to the module version folder; `gov.py analyze` runs the contracts; the stage commits (`{{ factory.naming.commit.stage }}`).
{% if stage.questions == 'forbidden' %}4. Ambiguity: non-breaking → ADR + continue; breaking → ADR `BLOCKED` + stop (`factory.ambiguity`). A `[QUESTION]` block from this stage is refused.
{% else %}4. Questions are allowed here and closed inside the dialogue with a recommended, researched answer; nothing is written to an external open-questions file.
